FFmpeg: push an HLS init section out from where the last read stopped.

Modified from FFmpeg 7.1.5 (LGPL-2.1-or-later, the FFmpeg developers), the release pinned in
dependencies.lock.json. Changed file: libavformat/hls.c. Backport of upstream commit f88f1041a6
("avformat/hls: advance the init section read pointer", 2026-09-29).

An init section longer than one read of the segment buffer was copied from its start on every
read, so its first chunk came out twice and corrupted what followed.

--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -1687,7 +1687,7 @@
     if (v->init_sec_buf_read_offset < v->init_sec_data_len) {
         /* Push init section out first before first actual segment */
         int copy_size = FFMIN(v->init_sec_data_len - v->init_sec_buf_read_offset, buf_size);
-        memcpy(buf, v->init_sec_buf, copy_size);
+        memcpy(buf, v->init_sec_buf + v->init_sec_buf_read_offset, copy_size);
         v->init_sec_buf_read_offset += copy_size;
         return copy_size;
     }
